## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of data footprint, latency budgets, and privacy controls for real-time collaboration features; also assesses ability to translate qualitative benefits into concrete, time-bound financial metrics.

## Key Concepts

- Delta encoding for presence data (cursor positions, editors yes/no)
- On-device aggregation to minimize network traffic
- Privacy/compliance considerations (opt-in, data minimization, retention)
- Latency budgets for real-time UI updates
- Cost modeling (server/storage, bandwidth) and break-even criteria

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: compute and emit deltapresence
function toDelta(prev, curr) {
  // compare and return only changed fields
  const delta = {};
  if (prev.userA !== curr.userA) delta.userA = curr.userA;
  // ... more fields
  return delta;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate the latency targets with simulated traffic?
- What edge cases (offline edits, rapid cursor moves) could break delta consistency?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to translate edge ML costs into a robust business case, including privacy constraints, rollout risk, and financial metrics.

## Key Concepts
- On-device RL inference energy and latency
- Policy delta encoding and secure transmission
- Drift/maintenance costs and OTA rollout
- Privacy/compliance and data minimization
- Rollout strategy and go/no-go criteria

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-cost estimator
function estimateCost(params) {
  const {
    dispatchesPerHour, energyPerDispatch, latencyMs,
    cloudSavingsPerDispatch
  } = params;
  // simplified calculation
  return energyPerDispatch * dispatchesPerHour / 3600;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate model drift in production and trigger rollback?
- What would you put in the go/no-go criteria to scale beyond pilot?

## Why This Question Is Asked
This question evaluates your understanding of on-device NLP trade-offs, privacy-by-design principles, and OTA update strategy—areas often underserved by conventional interview questions.

## Key Concepts
- **On-device ML**: Balancing model footprint against latency constraints
- **Privacy by design**: Minimizing cloud dependency for sensitive data
- **OTA updates**: Managing model versioning without disrupting user experience
- **Drift detection**: Monitoring perplexity and correction rate over time
- **Rollout strategy**: Phased deployment with clear go/no-go criteria

